# Definition of done

Do not claim work is complete, fixed, or passing until **every applicable item below is satisfied with evidence**. State the evidence (commands run + outcomes); if something is blocked, say so explicitly with the exact command the user must run. Evidence before assertions—always.

## Checklist (apply what's relevant to the change)

1. **Plan coverage** — every named step is implemented, tested, or explicitly blocked with a reason (`plan-execution.mdc`).
2. **Builds** — relevant crates build; `pnpm build` succeeds for frontend changes.
3. **Rust quality** — `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean (no new suppressions); no panics in non-test paths (`rust/rust-quality.mdc`).
4. **Frontend quality** — `pnpm lint` + `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` clean; no `any`/`console.log` introduced (`frontend-quality.mdc`).
5. **Tests** — the regression matrix rows for your change type pass; new behavior has tests; bug fixes have a guarding test (`regression-testing.mdc`). Report counts.
6. **Tenant isolation & RBAC** — new/changed queries/endpoints are tenant-scoped and permission-gated, with a cross-tenant denial test where applicable (`tenant-isolation.mdc`).
7. **Canonical schema sync** — if the `Event` shape changed, struct + JSON schema + TS types + migration are updated together and the drift check passes (`canonical-event-schema.mdc`).
8. **Migrations** — schema changes are new forward migration files only (`api-sqlx-migrations.mdc`).
9. **Audit & privacy** — mutations/security actions write audit rows; PII/GDPR handling respected; no PII or secrets in logs/error bodies (`audit-log-coverage.mdc`, `privacy-gdpr.mdc`).
10. **Docs** — inline `// Human:`/`// Agent:` comments added; public Rust items documented; README/ADR/OpenAPI updated when behavior or decisions changed (`inline-documentation.mdc`, `documentation.mdc`).
11. **No data-loss side effects** — nothing destructive was run without explicit permission (`data-safety.mdc`).

## Reporting

End substantive work with a short evidence summary: commands run and their results (e.g. `cargo test -p geos-api`: 42 passed; `pnpm build`: success; clippy: clean), plus any blocked items and how to unblock them. Do not say "done" without this.
